WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.170
- I watch the Oscars
because it lets me see

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:08.633
the human beings behind these
fantastical experiences.

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:11.219
- It celebrates the inner child

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:13.346
and the dreams of so many.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.973
- Since I was about
seven or eight years old,

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:16.891
I started going to the movies with my dad.

00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:19.644
- Growing up, as a kid, it
was always a dream of mine.

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:20.770
- I grew up with the Oscars.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.813
I always dreamed about

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:24.190
sort of being part of
this creative community.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.152
- Remember that you are part of a legacy,

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:30.238
that you're part of a world of filmmakers.

00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:33.158
- It's celebrating my community.

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:35.869
- It's just a very communal
experience, I guess,

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.912
with the rest of the world.

00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:42.292
- I'm in awe of all these
extraordinary people,

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:44.502
whether it's in front of the
camera or behind the camera.

00:00:44.502 --> 00:00:48.715
- I like seeing the joys of
people's names being called.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.549
- Alfonso Cuarón

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.717
(audience applauds)

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.551
- Rami Malek

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:52.719
- Lupita Nyong'o

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.848
- I love to see the best
day of someone's life,

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:58.641
and that's sometimes what you see.

00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:03.313
- Understanding that they are just people,

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.815
glamorous and ethereal as they are,

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.817
but they are just other people like me

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:11.029
is hugely empowering and encouraging.

00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:13.990
- It's a bit like that
movie Cinema Paradiso,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.784
about nostalgia.

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:17.410
- Italy for Cinema Paradiso!

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.870
(audience applauds)

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.789
- Going to the movies
and what it represents,

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.333
family or friends and
bringing people together,

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:26.044
and then of course, my experience
working in this industry.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.504
- Kind of like a opening the back door

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:30.173
and getting to look inside
and see what really goes on.

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:31.800
- Making something out of nothing.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.510
It's magic.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.470
- And I think that gives hope

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:38.473
to millions of potential
filmmakers around the world.

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:40.558
- It's wonderful to share those dreams.

